  "releaseNotes": "Modularization release. BREAKING CHANGES.\n\n            This package no longer carries its own copy of the onBIM Revit and BCL utility\n            libraries. It now depends on Revit.2025.Utils, which also brings\n            DotNetServicesForAECDevelopment transitively. Client code that used the types below\n            must update its using directives.\n\n            MOVED TO RevitUtils.* (from the Revit.2025.Utils dependency)\n\n            RevitUtils.Services: CategoryServices, DesignOptionServices, DocumentServices,\n            ElementIdServices, ElementServices, FamilyInstanceServices, GridServices,\n            ImportInstanceServices, LevelServices, RevitGeometryServices, TagCreationService,\n            TaskDialogServices, ViewServices, WallServices, Converters.\n\n            RevitUtils.Services.Collectors: CategoryCollectors, GenericCollectors,\n            LineStyleCollectors, PhaseCollectors, RoomCollectors, WallCollectors.\n\n            RevitUtils.Services.UnitsConversion: ConversionServices, SpecificFactorsServices,\n            UnitsServices.\n\n            RevitUtils.Entities: CompoundStructureLayersInfo, GetUnitsResultData,\n            MEPCurveReferences, SelectionSettings, TagInfo.\n\n            RevitUtils.Entities.ParametersHandlers: AccessParameterInfo, AccessParameterOptions,\n            ElementParameter, ElementParameterAccessor, ElementParameters, IElementParameters,\n            PropertyParameterBinding.\n\n            RevitUtils.Entities.PickSelectionFilters: CategorySelectionFilter,\n            MultiCategorySelectionFilter, NoFilter, PickSelectionFilter, WallSelectionFilter.\n\n            RevitUtils.Entities.Wrappers: ElementWrapper, FamilyInstanceWrapper, IElementWrapper,\n            IFamilyInstanceWrapper.\n\n            RevitUtils.Entities.EqualityComparers: ElementComparer, ElementReferenceComparer.\n\n            RevitUtils.Enums: AccessParameterMode, AccessParameterResult,\n            DoubleParameterConvertionMode, ElementParameterYesNoValue, ParameterDataType,\n            ParameterKind, ParameterValidationResult, RoofLineType.\n\n            MOVED TO DotNetServicesForAECDevelopment.* (transitive dependency)\n\n            Collections.EnumerableServices, Enumerations.EnumParser, Files.CSV, Files.Excel,\n            GenericServices.ObjectServices, MathServices.ArithmeticServices,\n            MathServices.RangeServices, MathServices.SequenceServices,\n            Reflection.ReflectionServices.\n\n            SECTION CREATION CLUSTER REMOVED\n\n            Axis, Section, SectionCreationData, WallElevation and CropRegionOffsetSettings were\n            dropped. Use the RevitUtils.Entities equivalents, which operate directly on\n            Autodesk.Revit.DB.XYZ instead of Dynamo geometry.\n\n            REMOVED WITH NO REPLACEMENT\n\n            ElementValidationServices (dead code), RevitGeometryServices.SwapCoordinateValue(XYZ),\n            FamilyInstanceServices.GetReferenceByName and .GetReferenceByType.\n\n            RENAMED IN THIS PACKAGE\n\n            DynamoForRevitUtils.Entities.AbstractGeometry: IAbstractGeometry is now\n            IVisualAbstractGeometry, AbstractGeometryBase is now VisualAbstractGeometry,\n            AbstractBoundingBox is now VisualBoundingBox, AbstractCoordinateSystem is now\n            VisualCoordinateSystem and AbstractVector is now VisualVector.\n\n            RevitElementsServices moved from Services.Dynamo to Services.RevitServices. The\n            Dynamo-typed members of WallServices are now in\n            Services.RevitServices.WallDynamoServices. RevitGeometryServices.ToProtoBoundingBox\n            and .CreateByRectangle are now in Services.Dynamo.BoundingBoxServices.\n\n            SIGNATURE CHANGES\n\n            CSV.Read now returns List<object[]> instead of IList, and CSV.Write now takes\n            List<object[]> instead of object[][]. This also changes the declared port types\n            of the CSVRead and CSVWrite nodes.\n\n            PACKAGING\n\n            The Revit API and Newtonsoft.Json assemblies are no longer embedded in this package;\n            they reach the client project through the Revit.2025.Utils dependency. MathNet.Numerics\n            is likewise no longer embedded and comes from its own package dependency. To avoid\n            assembly identity conflicts, the client project should not copy RevitAPI*.dll to its\n            own output folder.",
